<BaseLayout title="Projects | Bhagyashri Patil"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Projects / Case studies</span><h1>Work grounded in real problems.</h1><p>Selected projects and analytical approaches—not just lists of technologies.</p></header><section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Case study</span><div class="content-block"><h2>Performance Evaluation Metrics</h2><p><strong>Focus:</strong> Business intelligence · KPI design · Qlik dashboards</p><h3>The challenge</h3><p>At Valor Compounding Pharmacy, customer care performance was assessed primarily through prescriptions typed. Yet team members also handled calls, service issues, and doctor follow-ups, making one metric insufficient.</p><h3>The objective</h3><p>Design a balanced performance framework at the department, role, and individual level.</p><h3>Approach</h3><ul><li>Understand Central Fill, Direct to Patient, and shared customer-care workflows.</li><li>Consider prescriptions, phone interactions, Zendesk tickets, resolution times, and attendance.</li><li>Plan Qlik dashboards that give performance measures their proper context.</li></ul><h3>Intended deliverables</h3><p>A KPI framework and a series of Qlik dashboard views designed to support fairer performance conversations.</p><p><small>Quantified outcomes are intentionally omitted because they were not documented in the original project material.</small></p></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
